marsOceanShared.tsx READY (round 3, MarsVsOcean builder). Tokens: WATER{surface,mid,deep,darkest,murkLit,murkDark,murkShelf,murkDeep}, AMBER{top,foot,hot,bloom}, GRID{step 10, opacity 0.92, maxLat 80, poleFade 14, limbFade 0.85, width(k)} = the ONE "mapped" material, GRID_BLOOM (CSS filter), KEY_LIGHT [-0.62,0.56,0.46] (view space), NIGHT, ATMO{mars,earth}, MVO_TEX{mars, earth, earthOcean (R water, G shelf 1 shallow, B basin 0 coast..1 basin middle), earthGridLand (land minus islands < ~3.5 deg)}.
<LitGlobe texture cx cy r lon lat roll? light? ocean?={mask, reveal? (1 = ordinary surface, 0 = sunk murk; basin middles sink first), time?, glint? (0 = none), motes? (marine snow, ~0.3), coast? (shelf rim colour), lit?, dark?, shelf?, deep?} emissive?={src,color?,strength?} atmosphere? grade?={exposure,sat,warm,ambient,limb,highlight (0..1 shoulder for ice/cloud)} grid?={step,color?,opacity?,width?,landOnly?,mask?,maxLat?,poleFade?,limbFade?,glow?} layer?="globe"|"grid" width?=1080 height?=1920 style?/> (WebGL2 canvas, screen px; render with --gl=angle).
<GlobeGrid ...same view props... ocean?={mask} landOnly? landMask? (default MVO_TEX.earthGridLand) limbFade? (per globe) step? lineWidth? opacity?/> = static GRID on its own canvas with GRID_BLOOM; place right above its LitGlobe. The shader grid also cuts at the very limb (z < ~0.1).
<GlobeLines view={cx,cy,r,lon,lat,roll?} lines=[{pts:[lon,lat][],p}] color? width? opacity? bloom? limbFade? poleFade? heads? headLen?/> = draw-on lines (heads = a short hot head on drawing lines, no dots); same material when width=GRID.width(k), opacity=GRID.opacity, poleFade=GRID.poleFade.
projectGlobe(view,lon,lat)->{x,y,z>0 visible}; meridianLine(lon,fromLat?,toLat?), parallelLine(lat,fromLon,toLon).
Earth as used in MarsVsOcean: texture=MVO_TEX.earth, ocean={mask:MVO_TEX.earthOcean,time:frame,reveal,motes:0.3}, atmosphere=ATMO.earth, grade={exposure:1.05,sat:0.85,warm:0.05,ambient:0.05,limb:0.12,highlight:0.75}, + GlobeGrid landOnly limbFade=0.3 lineWidth=GRID.width(k); view lon -155 - 0.05 f, lat 10.
Changed in round 3 (all additive): grid.mask + MVO_TEX.earthGridLand, GlobeGrid landMask/limbFade, grade.highlight, ocean.coast/motes, GlobeLines heads are now short hot heads (headLen), WATER.murkDeep darker (#0E222B), earthOcean B channel softened.
